AB  - The proceedings contain 82 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Technology Enhanced Learning. The topics include: A social network analysis perspective of an online citizen inquiry community; developing mathematical thinking with scratch; facilitate sharing of training experience by exploring behavior discovery in trainees traces; using educational analytics to improve test performance; pedagogy, learning design and patterns of engagement; training workers for improving performance in crowdsourcing microtasks; engaging teaching professionals in design for online learning; a case study on mobile blended learning in higher education; an intelligent virtual reality environment for training pedestrian safety skills; improving automatic affect recognition on low-level speech features in intelligent tutoring systems; lessons learned from creating a mobile version of an educational board game to increase situational awareness; towards an integrated specialized learning application (ISLA) to support high functioning ASD children in mathematics learning; automatic tagging of learning objects based on their usage in web portal; on modeling learning communities; studying teacher orchestration load in technology-enhanced classrooms; towards reading session-based indicators in educational reading analytics; reflexive learning, socio-cognitive conflict and peer-assessment to improve the quality of feedbacks in online tests; a learning analytics approach to correlate the academic achievements of students with interaction data from an educational simulator; motivating learner engagement through explorable visual narratives; potentials of gamification in learning management systems; a framework to design educational mobile-based games across multiple spaces and grounding serious game design on scientific findings.
