AB  - The proceedings contain 183 papers. The topics discussed include: framing early alert of struggling students as an anomaly detection problem: an exploration; a systematic mapping on the use of data mining for the face-to-face school dropout problem; comprehensive empirical analysis of stop criteria in computerized adaptive testing; relative strengths of teachers and smart machines: towards an augmented task sharing; a neural network modelling and prediction of students’ progression in learning: a hybrid pedagogic method; experiments with auto-generated Socratic dialogue for source code understanding; factors that hinder in-service teachers from incorporating educational robotics into their daily or future teaching practice; Moroccan higher education at the time of covid-19: issues and challenges: a case study among master students business administration at IGA Casablanca; and students expectations on learning analytics: learning platform features supporting self-regulated learning.
