AB  - The proceedings contain 24 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Adaptive Instructional Systems. The topics include: Learning Within Gameplay Loops: Considering Adaptive Educational Technology from a Game Design Lens; toward a New Paradigm: Learning Analytics 2.0; considerations for Developing a Generalized Gradebook for an Open-Source Intelligent Tutoring System Framework; precision Learning Through Data Intelligence; learning to Take the Right Turn – Which Learning Media is Best Suited to Learn a Sequence of Actions to Solve a Rubik’s Cube?; towards a Vision of Standardized Competency-Based Training and Assessment Implementation; identifying Individual Differences that Predict Usage of an Adaptive Training System in a United States Marine Corps Course; which is Better Individualized Training for a Novel, Complex Task? Learner Control vs. Feedback Algorithms; stress and Coping with Task Difficulty: Investigating the Utility of a Micro-adaptive Aptitude Treatment Interaction Approach; exploring the Individual Differences in Multidimensional Evolution of Knowledge States of Learners; not All Pain Leads to Gain: The Role of Learner Engagement in Adaptive Flashcard Training; ibigkas! Math 2.0: An Intelligent Computer-Supported Collaborative Learning Application for Grade 5 Mathematics; teaching Diffusion of Innovations Involving Technology Startups Using Agent-Based Simulation Modeling: Architecture and Design Considerations; iterative Improvement of Automatically Generated Practice with the Content Improvement Service; merging Human and Non-human (System) Data to Describe Students’ Adaptive Learning Experience in Postsecondary Gateway Math Courses; towards Application of Adaptive Instructional Systems in Simulation-Based Lifeboat Training Using Bayesian Networks; trust Acceptance Mapping - Designing Intelligent Systems for Use in an Educational Context; human Performance Data Lifecycle Management as a Foundation for Adaptive Training.
