AB  - The societal movement toward smart, personalized healthcare highlights the need to protect the individual privacy of people in utilizing machine learning. In this paper, we introduce a new system called Federated Multi-Layered Deep Neural Network with Adaptive Hyperparameter Optimization (Fed-MLDNN-AHPO) which combines federated learning, metaheuristic optimization, and Biogeography Based Optimization (BBO) to apply to deep neural networks with sensitive healthcare data. It has the capacity to apply training processes from across multiple locations to comply with privacy-related legislation such as HIPAA and GDPR. Moreover, the adaptive tuning works with data from the customer which is heterogeneous and not consistently independent and identically distributed (IID). Applications are demonstrated and evaluated from datasets from eICU, FeTS, MIMIC-III, and BRATS20. Various approaches were considered from this novel system to be very effective in classification and segmentation performance over baseline approaches. Furthermore, we have implemented modules for explainability and fairness to support trust in AI in healthcare. Thus, Fed-MLDNN-AHPO allows the implementation of safe, understandable, and scalable privacy-preserving intelligence in the healthcare domain.
