AB  - Federated Learning (FL) enables decentralized model training across heterogeneous data sources with a focus on privacy. However, regulatory compliance and governance remain underdeveloped. This paper proposes the Federated Cognitive Infrastructure (FCI)—a novel framework that integrates Reinforcement Learning (RL) agents for real-time, adaptive governance in federated AI. FCI leverages semantic data contracts, hierarchical RL-based control, and modular Explainable AI (XAI) to automate compliance with evolving regulations like GDPR and HIPAA. Evaluations on insurance and synthetic healthcare data show improved compliance, fairness, interpretability, and model performance, advancing privacy-aware AI in regulated domains.
