AB  - Smarttutoring systems and adaptive learning technologies are transforming the landscape of education by offering personalized and dynamic learning experiences. These systems leverage Automated learning algorithms and artificial intelligence (AI) to assess students' progress, identify learning gaps, and tailor instructional content to meet individual needs. Smart tutoring systems aim to mimic the guidance of human tutors, providing instant feedback, personalized problemsolving approaches, and adaptive challenges to students, while adjusting the difficulty level based on performance. In parallel, adaptive learning platforms enable real-time customization of learning pathways, ensuring that students are presented with the most relevant content at each stage of their educational journey. This paper explores the key principles and technologies behind smart tutoring and adaptive learning, highlighting their potential to enhance student engagement, improve learning outcomes, and promote self-directed learning. Furthermore, the challenges associated with implementing these systems, such as data privacy concerns, system scalability, and accessibility, are discussed. © 2025 IEEE.
