AB  - Intelligent Tutoring Systems (ITS) have transformed the online learning scenario, but in many ways are lacking a certain explainability and a high level of personalization, hindering trust and engagement among learners. A humanistic framework for AI tutoring that combines explainable AI and adaptive learning approaches, aiming to enhance cognitive and emotional learning processes. The system uses a Weighted Learner Vector (WLV) as a profiler, SHAP and LIME for transparent feedback, and its instructional plan is powered with reinforcement learning. Training and validation were done using the EdNet data, whereas Unity ML-Agents were used to simulate it in real time. An analysis of experimental data indicates 42.2 percent improvement of learner engagement, 65.2 percent decrease of misconceptions, and an average 30% gain of post-test scores. The system also demonstrated a 68.3% decrease in latency, a Feedback Trust Index of 0.902, and high emotional adaptability. These results demonstrate that the system has the potential to provide successful, credible, and individualized tutoring sessions to various populations of learners.  © 2025 IEEE.
