AB  - Artificial Intelligence (AI) is no longer a distant concept confined to theoretical discourse; it has become a transformative force within classrooms across the globe. This chapter critically explores the evolution of AI in education, tracing its journey from speculative theory to practical deployment. With a reflective lens, it examines how AI- driven systems have reshaped pedagogical methodologies, from personalized learning environments and adaptive assessments to the nuanced roles of intelligent tutoring and learning analytics. Beyond the promise of efficiency and customization, the chapter grapples with ethical dilemmas, pedagogical dependencies, and the socioemotional implications of AI- mediated instruction. Ultimately, it argues for a more human- centered, ethically conscious path forward-one where technology supports, rather than supplants, the relational and transformative essence of education. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
