AB  - Educational Data Mining (EDM) has emerged as a highly significant field for evaluating complex educational datasets in order to enhance learning and facilitate efficient decision-making. When compared to other automated ways for analyzing multidimensional and multifarious educational data, traditional machine learning techniques have demonstrated limited effectiveness. This study presents a Hybrid Deep Learning Approach for Classification and Recommendation in EDM, which records spatial and temporal trends using Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN) and Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks for educational data. The suggested model makes use of feature selection techniques, which simplify the data and improve prediction accuracy. The hybrid architecture was trained using real-world educational datasets, which comprise assessment data, learning activities, and student performance statistics. Additionally, by recommending relevant learning materials, the recommendation systems achieved their goals of raising students' academic engagement. Collectively, these results highlight the function of hybrid deep learning methods used in EDM for individualized learning, intelligent tutoring, and institutional assessment and planning systems. Future work aims to improve the model utilizing explainable AI and reinforcement learning since they have the ability to increase flexibility and clarity in decision making in the current environment.  © 2025 IEEE.
