AB  - The implementation of AI to the very process of learning, particularly the heart of active learning in the engineering field. The use of AI-driven triggering virtual labs is a new innovative idea that may help students to study more interactively, immersively, and most importantly on a larger scale. Working in these laboratories, AI-based simulations, along with augmented reality, virtual reality, and intelligent tutoring systems, are implemented to recreate complex engineering experiments and give real-time feedbacks. The literature on AI-enabled virtual labs in the teaching and learning of engineering has not yet provided a comprehensive coverage of the advantages, disadvantages, and opportunities of the technology. The traditional engineering engineering laboratories are priceless yet present complications like the prohibitive price, scarcity of equipment and security issues. Virtual labs based on AI can solve these problems with a cost-efficient, flexible, and scalable solution. They are safe spaces where students can play around, in which AI algorithms replicate with precision the behavior of an actual physical matter, whether whether it is a blend of substances or collection of circuits or mechanical systems. Moreover, these virtual labs are accessible anywhere, which makes them the perfect solution to the students who do not have access to physical lab. Personalized learning experience with the use of AI-enabled virtual labs is one of the most promising things. Such adaptive learning AIs examine student interactions on more detailed level to identify the knowledge level gap and adjust the complexity of experiment presented, to suit the needs of that student. They will save time and effort when smart feedback loops are integrated because they will be given on-the-go support to learn complex engineering concepts. Also, AI virtual assistants and chatbots are also mentors to the students as they are performing experiments and can pose some questions as though the person was a human instructor. Machine learning and data analytics capabilities, which are part of the virtual experience, are another important component. According to these technologies, performance monitoring, predictive evaluation, learning analytics, and so on are conducted to assist teachers in adjusting to the approaches of teaching. By tracking students' logs of what they do and how they perform, AI can reveal common misconceptions and suggest interventions that can be carried out on an individual basis or at scale. © 2025 IEEE.
