AB  - In the context of the development of intelligent education and personalized learning, although Multimodal Learning Analytics (MMLA) brings opportunities for building learner profiles, there is a “recognition intervention gap”, and existing systems are difficult to realize their value in real teaching scenarios. To address this issue, this article proposes the “Hierarchical Cross Modal Attention Fusion and Dynamic Intervention Network” (MAFDIN) end-to-end deep learning framework, forming an intelligent closed-loop of “perception decision action”. The MAFDIN framework has two core innovations. Firstly, the Hierarchical Cross Modal Attention (HCMA) module can dynamically balance the importance of information within and between different data modalities, achieving more reliable and interpretable feature fusion and learning state recognition. Secondly, the Dynamic Intervention Strategy Network (DIPN) based on reinforcement learning takes state recognition results as input to learn the optimal teaching intervention strategy. The main contribution of this article is to propose an innovative hierarchical fusion architecture HCMA, which significantly improves the accuracy of student state recognition under multimodal data; Design and implement an end-to-end MMLA framework DIPN that combines state recognition with reinforcement learning intervention decision-making; Through experimental verification, MAFDIN outperforms mainstream baseline models in state recognition performance, and its dynamic intervention mechanism can effectively improve students’ negative learning state. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s)
