AB  - The integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in higher education is transforming instructional design, learner engagement, and institutional operations. This paper provides a comprehensive review of AI applications in university teaching and learning, including personalized learning environments, automated assessment systems, intelligent tutoring platforms, and predictive analytics. Drawing upon contemporary literature and empirical findings, we map current research trends and technological advancements, such as large language models, multimodal AI, and adaptive learning systems, and identify associated pedagogical benefits and ethical challenges. To address the growing need for principled AI deployment, we propose a novel Three-Layer Framework for Responsible AI Integration, which encompasses technological infrastructure, pedagogical functionality, and ethical governance. This framework offers practical guidance for educators, researchers, and policymakers seeking to implement AI in higher education in a context-sensitive, equitable, and pedagogically sound manner. © 2025 IEEE.
