AB  - The rapid expansion of artificial intelligence (AI), big data, and digital platforms is reshaping how governments design and deliver public services. While these technologies offer opportunities for efficiency, transparency, and evidence-based policy making, they also raise significant concerns regarding privacy, cyber security, and public trust. This study examines the concept of trustworthy smart governments within the broader context of digital transformation and increasing datafication of governance systems. It explores how institutional safeguards, ethical AI frameworks, and robust cyber security infrastructures can strengthen accountability and legitimacy in digitally enabled public administration. Particular attention is given to data governance, algorithmic transparency, and citizen participation as essential components of trustworthy digital states. Copyright © 2027, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. Copying or distributing in print or electronic forms without written permission of IGI Global Scientific Publishing is prohibited. Use of this chapter to train generative artificial intelligence (AI) technologies is expressly prohibited. The publisher reserves all rights to license its use for generative AI training and machine learning model development.
