AB  - In the past few years, the need for smart banking systems and fraud detection has changed significantly. However, traditional methods of fraud detection using Artificial Intelligence (AI) are mainly based on static Machine Learning (ML) algorithms including identifying hidden relationships among transactions, coping with continuously varying behaviors of fraudsters, and providing privacy preserving collaborative banking intelligence among multiple institutions. To address these challenges a new framework namely Federated Temporal Graph Reinforcement Learning (FTGRL) is developed for fraud detection within smart banking applications. Moreover, this framework starts with the utilization of preprocessing techniques for development of the characteristics of fraud sensitive transactions and to reduce data imbalance issues. This is followed by the utilization of Temporal Graph Neural Networks (TGNN) to generate deep temporal representations of transactions by identifying suspicious patterns of transactions between customers and hidden relationships among customers. After that, the Federated Learning (FL) concept allows several banking institutions to collaborate on developing fraud detection policies without having to disclose sensitive customer information. Experimental results demonstrated that the proposed FTGRL framework attained greater in terms of accuracy of 99.96% compared to existing Ensemble Independent Bagging Machine Learning Classifier (EIBMC) framework.
