AB  - This study addresses persistent instructional challenges in the “Basic French” course, including heavy teacher workload, delayed feedback, fragmented learning analytics, and limited opportunities for oral communication. The purpose of this research is to design and implement an AI-supported blended learning model integrating the Chaoxing AI Workbench, a French Assistant dialogue system, and the DeepSeek large language model, and to evaluate through machine learning the key AI-assisted factors that influence learner satisfaction. Questionnaire data (N = 200) were analyzed using a logistic regression model to quantify how perceptions of various AI-assisted learning features contribute to satisfaction. The model achieved strong performance (AUC = 0.841, Accuracy = 0.717). Results indicate that AI-based personalized Q&A support is the strongest positive predictor of learner satisfaction, while AI reliability shows marginal positive effects. Personalized content shows a marginal negative effect, suggesting a mismatch between AI-generated recommendations and learner expectations. These findings demonstrate the significance of AI-driven personalization and feedback in language learning and provide direction for optimizing AI-enhanced French instruction. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
