AB  - Human–AI collaboration in education marks a significant paradigm shift in how teaching, learning, and knowledge creation are designed and experienced. Rather than replacing educators or diminishing human agency, artificial intelligence increasingly functions as an enabling partner that augments human capabilities. This collaboration reshapes the traditional roles of educators from information transmitters to learning designers, facilitators, mentors, and ethical stewards who guide the responsible use of AI-driven tools. AI applications such as adaptive learning platforms, learning analytics, intelligent tutoring systems, and generative technologies enable customized feedback, inclusive learning environments, and competency-based progression. However, the effectiveness of human–AI collaboration depends not merely on technological sophistication but on thoughtful pedagogical integration grounded in equity, transparency, and academic integrity. Critical challenges including algorithmic bias, data privacy, digital divides, and overreliance on automation, necessitate robust governance. Copyright © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing.
