AB  - In the context of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), particularly the goal of E Quality Education, higher education institutions face increasing demands to provide inclusive, effective, and personalized learning support. Traditional instructional models struggle to meet the diverse learning needs and behavioral patterns of contemporary university students. To address this challenge, this study proposes a deep learning-based personalized intelligent tutoring system that integrates Depthwise Separable Convolution, Gated Recurrent Units (GRU), and Variational Autoencoders (VAE), optimized through the Whale Optimization Algorithm (WOA). Using real student data, the system models learning behaviors, extracts high-dimensional features, and generates adaptive learning recommendations. Experimental results demonstrate significant improvements in prediction accuracy, computational efficiency, and model scalability compared with traditional approaches. The findings show that deep learning can play a crucial role in advancing personalized learning and supporting the educational transformation envisioned by the SDGs, offering practical pathways toward more intelligent, equitable, and sustainable higher education systems.  © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
