AB  - Agentic artificial intelligence is beginning to take its place as a new paradigm in educational technology; it builds upon previous paradigms of adaptive learning platforms and intelligent tutoring systems by adding autonomous, goal-oriented agents capable of planning, acting and coordinating amongst a variety of tools.Studies on adaptive learning have already demonstrated that AI-based systems can customize the sequencing, pacing and feedback of content by or to learners, enhancing engagement and performance when high-quality learner models are integrated with sound pedagogical principles. Recent efforts in the field of large language models, multi-Agent systems and agentic AI systems suggest a transition in development toward single intelligent elements and towards coordinated groups of agents acting on top of learning analytics, knowledge tracing models and rich content repositories. This survey summarises the recent research on AI-Assisted adaptive learning, intelligent tutoring systems, large language model-based tutoring and explicitly agentic educational systems, and how these strands are integrated to agentic AI-powered adaptive learning systems.It is analyzed in terms of typical architectural designs, forms of adaptivity, educational benefits reported, and continued challenges, such as cold-start issues, transparency, bias, data governance and human supervision requirements. The survey ends by noting a gap in the empirical research on fully agentic platforms, and future research opportunities on an open research agenda in the future of scalable, trustworthy and pedagogically motivated agentic AI-based adaptive learning. © 2026 IEEE.
