AB  - As artificial intelligence (AI) becomes pervasive in education, data literacy has emerged as a foundational competence in AI-mediated learning. Despite increasing research attention, the field remains fragmented, with limited longitudinal evidence on its thematic structure and evolution. Addressing this gap, this study presents a longitudinal analysis of AI and data literacy research from 2005 to 2025 using BERT-based and dynamic topic modeling. Twelve topic clusters were identified, revealing conceptual relationships, temporal trajectories, and citation patterns. Findings show rapid growth in topics related to intelligent tutoring systems, learning analytics, ethics, and evaluation-oriented data literacy, particularly following the rise of generative AI. Keyword network analysis indicates a shift from data mining and visualization toward AI-driven analytics and educational innovation. © 2026 ISTE+ASCD.
