AB  - Emerging technologies are transforming language education by offering personalized, adaptive, and data-driven learning experiences. Natural Language Processing (NLP) enables the development of intelligent language tools such as chatbots, automated feedback systems, and pronunciation analyzers, which support learners in acquiring linguistic skills efficiently. Learning analytics harness student interaction data to monitor progress, identify learning gaps, and inform targeted interventions, enhancing both teaching effectiveness and learner outcomes. Intelligent Tutoring Systems (ITS) provide adaptive scaffolding, individualized instruction, and real-time feedback, promoting active engagement and self-directed learning. The integration of these technologies fosters a learner-centered environment, supports diverse learning styles, and facilitates the acquisition of communicative competence across cultural and linguistic contexts. Copyright ©2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. Copying or distributing in print or electronic forms without written permission of IGI Global Scientific Publishingis prohibited. Use of this chapter to train generative artificial intelligence (AI) technologies is expressly prohibited. The publisher reserves all rights to license its use for generative AI training and machine learning model development.
