AB  - The emergence of intelligent and personalized digital education and the shortcomings of the conventional language teaching system including conventional learning resources and conventional teaching techniques are apparent. The necessity of personalized and intelligent digital education has exposed the shortcomings of conventional language teaching systems that mainly use static learning resources and teaching techniques that do not take into consideration any difference between students. In order to solve these shortcomings, in this paper, the Intelligent Adaptive Learning Framework for Uzbek Language Teaching Using Dynamic Parameter Adaptation (IALF-DPA) is proposed. The uniqueness of the proposed framework is that it incorporates continuous learner profiling, attention-based deep learning to predict learner's performance, adaptive content recommendation and dynamic parameter adaptation (DPA) technique which continuously adapts the level of difficulty of the lesson, order of content delivery and revision schedule according to learner's performance in real time. Unlike existing adaptive learning frameworks which are based on predefined adaptation rules, it constantly adapts the instructional parameters according to the learner's accuracy, reaction time, error pattern and knowledge acquisition. The proposed framework was evaluated using the benchmark data set of Uzbek language learning which had vocabulary, grammar, reading, and writing tests conducted among learners of different skill levels. The experimental evaluation of the proposed IALF-DPA system indicates that the suggested system has achieved higher accuracy (97.84%), higher precision (97.32%), higher recall (97.11%), higher F1-score (97.21%), higher learner completion rate (95.68%), and higher knowledge retention rate (95.13%) as compared to the existing approaches of adaptive learning. Thus, the above results validate that the use of DPA helps to increase the engagement and effectiveness of learning in intelligent Uzbek language teaching and learning. © 2026, International Academic Institute for Science and Technology. All rights reserved.
