AB  - The proceedings contain 132 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Artificial Intelligence in Education. The topics include: The Mediating Mirror: A Recursive Symbolic Production Model for GenAI-Mediated Language Learning; Evaluating Pedagogical Styles of LLM-Generated Hint Sets; a Near-Peer Reflective Agent for K-12 Collaborative Problem-Solving; Seeing Like a Student: Difficulty and Error Alignment of MLLMs on Visual Math Problems; modeling Embodied Collaborative Problem-Solving Dynamics in Immersive Virtual Reality; Teachers Personalizing Lesson Plans and Tasks Using GenAI; Academic Practice and Generative AI: Configurations of Work in Two Mexican Universities; Diagnosing When to Trust AI Coding of Student-Generated Text: A Committee-Based Framework for Characterizing Uncertainty in LLM Annotation Systems; Contingent Support with LLM-Based Scaffolding for Collaborative Problem Solving in an Inquiry-Based Game Environment; From Competence Structures to Formative Feedback: A Knowledge Space Theory Pipeline for Evaluating and Enhancing LLM-Based Learning Recommendations; automating the Identification of the Triggers of Socially Shared Metacognitive Regulation in Ill-Structured Collaborative Problem-Solving: A Multimodal Analysis Approach; from Assessment to Tutoring: Evidence-Led Faithfulness for Goal-Oriented Singing Practice; A Case Study with an Intelligent Tutoring System for Active Study of Worked Examples in Introductory JAVA Programming; comparing Multimodal Learning Analytics Pipelines and Multimodal Large Language Models for Detecting Collaborative Engagement in Science Simulations; Generative AI in Secondary Education Across Diverse Populations; preface; AI4CAREER: Responsible AI for STEM Career Development at Scale in K-16 Education; modeling Dynamics of Learning and Learners with the Transition Network Analysis Toolkit; Designing and Evaluating Next-Generation Learning Interfaces: Linking AI, HCI, and the Learning Sciences; 10th Educational Data Mining in Computer Science Education (CSEDM) Workshop; HAI-Agency: Workshop on Orchestrating Human and AI Agency for Proactive and Reflective Learning; I Workshop on AIED Unplugged.
