AB  - To address current deficiencies in Linux educational platforms—including inadequate personalized learning analytics, insufficient optimization of data-informed pedagogy, and limited algorithmic capabilities for adaptive instruction—a big data-powered Linux educational system has been developed. The platform incorporates machine learning models for analyzing learner behaviors, applies data mining methodologies for uncovering knowledge patterns, and leverages artificial intelligence for generating personalized learning trajectory recommendations. Drawing upon Linux system architecture principles integrated with big data processing frameworks, the application tier utilizes distributed computing infrastructure featuring Hadoop ecosystem compatibility, capabilities for real-time data manipulation, and an extensive learning analytics interface. The system employs deep learning models for forecasting student achievement, applies clustering methodologies for categorizing learners, and delivers intelligent guidance via natural language processing technologies. Furthermore, an instructional system founded on video information transmission, decoding, and playback has been designed and incorporated into pedagogical practices. Assessment of teaching outcomes demonstrates favorable openness and compatibility characteristics. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
