AB  - The proceedings contain 50 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Intelligent Computing and Communication. The topics include: Multi-Model Tweets Analysis for Understanding AI Literacy Using Natural Language Processing and Deep Learning; towards Container Migration Resilience in Diverse IoT Edge Environments; stored Cross-Site Scripting to Session Hijacking: Demonstration and Defensive Analysis; Adversarial Robustness Evaluation of CNNs: A Case Study of Black-Box Attacks with Defenses; optimizing Artificial Intelligence for Sustainability: Computational Efficiency and Green Metrics; Privacy-Preserving Federated Learning with Federated GANs for Early Heart Disease Prediction; Forensic Deepfake Audio Detection Using CNN-Attention Mechanism; Advanced Lung Nodule Malignancy Classification Using Multi-scale 3D CNN with Radiomics-Augmented Features and Explainable Artificial Intelligence; Enhancing Fair Play in Fantasy Sports: The Role of Explainable AI in Team Selection; beyond Peaks: Deep Temporal Models for Ocular Electrophysiology; MOON-Fed: A Model-Contrastive Federated Learning Framework for Efficient Software Defect Prediction; Managing QUIC at Scale: DoS Robustness, Observability, and CID-Aware Load Balancing; AI-Driven IoT Framework for Predictive Healthcare Monitoring Using Wearable Sensors; AI-Powered System for Missing Person Identification Using Age-Invariant Face Recognition; Energy-Aware VM migration in Cloud-Computing Optimization; Network Intrusion Detection for Vulnerable Networks Using CICIDS2017: Preprocessing, SMOTE Balancing, and Comparative Evaluation of Random Forest, XGBoost and Neural Network; use of Ensemble Learners to Predict Number of Defects in a Software; mental Health and Well-Being Surveillance, Assessment, and Tracking Solution Among Children; Leveraging Intelligent Tutoring Systems and AI Analytics for Personalized Classroom Management and Student Engagement; machine Learning-Based Predictive Modeling and Visualization for Early Breast Cancer Diagnosis Using Open-Source Clinical Data; A Review of Contrastive Learning for Stress and Anxiety Detection Using EDA and BVP Signals.
