AB  - A single teaching method cannot fit all students' needs, as the increase of digital learning spaces has been lightly proved. According to this, tailored education is recognized as a promising paradigm to enhance learning effectiveness by customizing education paths and content for each learner based on his or her own individual profile. Therefore, AI has been extensively investigated as a technology that can be applied to the development of Adaptive Learning (AL) systems that are capable of handling the personalization process on a large scale. In this paper, we examine the AI-enabled AL systems in the context of personalized learning, and we present an evaluation of them. It covers existing techniques, such as machine learning and high-level AI techniques. It analyses the pros and cons of how transparent the two are as systems, how pedagogically relevant they are, and how effective they are in terms of personalization. This reflection opens up avenues for researching the design of more transparent, robust, and learnercentered adaptive learning systems and reveals substantial underexplored research areas. This will help the researchers and practitioners to learn about the trends and the gaps existent in personalized education. © 2026 IEEE.
