AB  - Reading comprehension is a very important part of language learning and academic performance development and Intelligent Tutoring Systems are used to help to develop it more and more often. Conventional ITS based on deep learning models such as BERT and RoBERTa are highly accurate at performing question answering but lack interpretability. This black-box property prevents learners and educators to believe or comprehend the decisions of the system hence; the system has limited educational value. This issue can be resolved with the help of the introduction of X-RoBERTa, a new framework that combines a high-performing RoBERTa model and SHAP, an Explainable AI method. The goal is not only to give the correct answers but also to give, at the token level, what the reasons the model used to produce its answer were. Such two-fold operation enhances trust, participation, and comprehension of pattern of reasoning among learners. The working process includes entering a question and a passage in the X-RoBERTa operating system that suggests the correct answer span and points significant words by SHAP values. This is presented graphically to the learner in a simple manner. Based on experimental results, the proposed model exhibits an accuracy of 98.5 percent, with an explanation quality of 98.4 percent. The system could be extended in the future by multilingual integration, emotion-sensitive feedback, and dynamic learning screens so that the teaching can be even more individualized and to improve overall learning experience. © 2026 IEEE.
