AB  - Incorporation of artificial intelligence (AI) into the educational landscape has changed the way learning was traditionally done, which has allowed personalized and adaptive approaches to learning. AI-driven Intelligent Tutoring Systems (ITS) can also be useful in facilitating classroom management and interaction with students by offering a customized learning experience and immediate feedback. The given work aims at using AI-based ITS and learning analytics to track the engagement, make predictions, and assist teachers in making data-driven decisions. Based on EdNet, ASSISTments, and Khan Academy-inspired datasets, several features, including engagement score, tutoring session, and academic performance indicators, were examined. Machine learning predictive modeling was implemented to identify dropout risks and other factors that play significant roles in learning outcomes. The findings prove that the interaction levels are greatly dependent on time of the day, and the most interaction was recorded in the afternoon. On average, the increase in academic points was 15 points with the help of AI tutoring. The engagement score and the final grades were weakly related (r = 0.71). The prediction model of dropouts had a dropout accuracy of 91 percent with engagement score and baseline performance turning out to be the most significant factors. These results demonstrate that AI-sensitive ITS can significantly contribute to classroom activities and target support teachers in implementing specific interventions to improve learning outcomes. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
